.TH SUFFIX 1 2026-08-07 "Suffix 0.1.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
suffix \- manage durable short links on domains you own
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B suffix
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B suffix man install
.RI [ --dir " man1-directory" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Stored Business photos and uploaded files may be protected with
.BR --protect .
The password is prompted without echo. Use
.B --password-file PATH
for automation. Photo protection applies to local mode and ?L, not ?R.
.B suffix
is the command-line client for the Suffix canonical API at
.B https://suffix.org/api/v1.
It manages only the domains and shortcuts belonging to the active saved account.
Use
.B suffix login
to approve and store a bearer key through the browser.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B login [email]
Select or create a saved profile for the optional email. A matching saved key is
reused without opening the browser. Use
.B --renew
to open the browser and replace that key intentionally.
Old unnamed default profiles are discarded; sign in again with an email or an
explicit profile name.
.TP
.B ls [options] [account]
List shortcuts. The normal output is tab-separated shortcut and destination
columns. A trailing saved account email selects that account
without changing the active profile.
.TP
.B search \fIregexp\fR [\fIaccount\fR]
Search both short URLs and destination targets with a case-insensitive regular
expression. Output is tab-separated match scope, shortcut, and target.
.TP
.B add [options] \fIvalue\fR [\fItail\fR] [\fItarget-url\fR]
Create a shortcut. Use a hostname-and-tail value such as
.B pair.rs/typesec
or use
.B -d
with an explicit domain hostname. Top-tier accounts may pass
.B --photo
and choose
.B --photo-mode local|remote.
Local mode asks the service to store and directly serve a managed image copy;
remote mode resolves to the original and is the default. On a public Photo URL,
.B ?L
and
.B ?R
override the saved mode for one request.
Before creation, Suffix offers to reuse an existing shortcut for the same
target or edit an occupied tail. Scripts must opt in with
.B --allow-duplicate-target
or
.B --edit-existing.
.PP
Every account can use the public
.B suf.cx
base without attaching a domain. Use
.B suffix add --public URL
to choose a shortest available candidate. Combine
.BR --letters ,
.BR --alphanumeric ,
and
.BR --words
to select candidate styles, or use
.B suffix add --public TAIL URL
to request a custom tail.
.TP
.B edit \fIshortcut-id\fR [--tail \fItail\fR] [--target-url \fIurl\fR] [--title \fIlabel\fR] [--active \fIbool\fR]
Edit selected shortcut fields. If no version is supplied, Suffix reads it first.
.TP
.B photo \fIshortcut-id\fR (-l|--local|-r|--remote|--drop) [--version \fIversion\fR]
Change the saved serving mode of an existing Photo shortcut, or remove its
managed image with
.BR --drop .
If no version is supplied, Suffix reads it before updating.
.TP
.B password \fIshortcut-id\fR (--add|--remove) [--password-file \fIpath\fR]
Add, change, or remove password protection on a stored photo or managed file.
Without a password file, adding prompts securely without echo.
.TP
.B upload [options] \fIhost/tail file\fR [\fIaccount\fR]
Upload a Business file, up to 100 MB, into the account-scoped Suffix Blob store
and create a shortcut that downloads it. Deleting the shortcut removes the
managed object. Use
.B -d \fIhost tail file\fR
for an explicit hostname.
.TP
.B rm \fIshortcut-id\fR [--version \fIversion\fR]
Delete a shortcut. If no version is supplied, Suffix reads it before deleting.
.TP
.B domain ls|add|rm
List, add, or remove owned domains. A trailing saved account email selects that
account. The same trailing account convention applies to
.B add,
.B rm,
and
.B stats.
.TP
.B transfer \fIdomain\fR [--to \fIemail\fR]
Create a short-lived code for moving a domain to another account.
.TP
.B accept \fIcode\fR
Accept a domain-transfer code into the active account.
.TP
.B mv [--to|--from] \fIdomain\fR \fIaccount\fR
Move a domain between two saved accounts. By default, or with
.B --to,
move from the active account to the named account. With
.B --from,
move from the named account to the active account. Supplying a second account
uses the explicit source-and-target form.
.TP
.B account [ls|add|rm|name]
List, add, remove, or select saved account profiles.
.TP
.B man install [--dir \fIman1-directory\fR]
Install this manual as
.I suffix.1
in the first writable standard section-1 manual directory. On macOS, Suffix
checks Homebrew, local, and user-local directories. On Linux, it checks local,
user-local, and system directories. Use
.B --dir
to select an exact directory. A system-owned destination may require elevated
privileges.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B suffix/config.toml
The platform configuration directory holds saved API bases, account metadata,
and API keys.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SUFFIX_API_BASE
Overrides the saved API base URL.
.TP
.B SUFFIX_API_KEY
Overrides the saved bearer API key.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B suffix
exits zero on success and nonzero for invalid arguments or authentication,
API, and manual-page installation failures.
.SH SEE ALSO
The Suffix dashboard and API documentation are available at
.B https://suffix.org.
